00:01:39.025 --> 00:01:43.257
know when she needs a doctor." Moncharmin began walking Raoul toward the door. "But—"

15
00:01:43.258 --> 00:01:53.203
"Good day, monsieur." Moncharmin closed the office door in Raoul's face. Raoul stood at the door for a minute, thinking. Christine did not want to see him, as she'd

16
00:01:53.204 --> 00:02:00.998
made clear in her note, but Mama Valerius might talk to him. From what

17
00:02:00.999 --> 00:02:12.389
Raoul had seen at the seaside and in Christine's dressing room, he believed Christine

18
00:02:13.521 --> 00:02:24.368
was the victim of some unscrupulous person. But who? At Mama Valerius' apartment, a maid

19
00:02:24.369 --> 00:02:32.752
answered the door and showed Raoul into a small drawing room. Returning a few

20
00:02:32.753 --> 00:02:41.075
minutes later, she said, "Madame apologizes that she must see you in her bedroom

21
00:02:41.406 --> 00:02:46.265
because she can no longer walk." The maid ushered Raoul into Mama Valerius' bedroom. "Ah,

22
00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:53.022
Monsieur de Chagny, it's been many years since we were together in Perros-Guirec!" Mama

23
00:02:53.023 --> 00:02:59.890
Valerius extended both her hands to Raoul, who gazed into her kind face. "I'm an

24
00:02:59.891 --> 00:03:06.633
old widow now, but heaven has sent you, so that we can talk of

25
00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:14.300
Christine." "Yes!" Raoul said eagerly. "Where is Christine? No one has seen her for

26
00:03:15.374 --> 00:03:21.994
almost two weeks." "She sent me a note that she's with her Angel of Music,"

27
00:03:21.995 --> 00:03:28.056
the old woman replied. Raoul dropped into a chair. "Really? Her Angel of Music?"

28
00:03:28.057 --> 00:03:33.177
Mama Valerius smiled at him and put a finger to her lips. "You mustn't

29
00:03:33.178 --> 00:03:40.346
tell anyone. I'm very fond of you, and so is Christine." "What makes you think

30
00:03:40.347 --> 00:03:43.247
she's fond of me?" "She used to speak of you every day and .

31
00:03:43.248 --> 00:03:51.501
. ." Mama Valerius leaned forward as if telling Raoul a secret. "She told me

32
00:03:51.502 --> 00:04:04.846
that in Perros-Guirec you said you couldn't live without her. Oh, silly boy!" Mama

33
00:04:04.847 --> 00:04:09.369
Valerius laughed heartily. Raoul sprang from his chair, blushing with embarrassment. "Where are you

34
00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:22.332
going?" Mama Valerius asked. "Sit down again at once. I'm sorry I laughed—did you think she was free to marry?" "Are you saying Christine is engaged to someone else?"

35
00:04:22.712 --> 00:04:30.234
Raoul asked, his voice choking with emotion. "No, you know as well as I

36
00:04:30.235 --> 00:04:37.448
do that Christine can't marry even if she wants to." "I don't know anything about

37
00:04:37.449 --> 00:04:42.901
this at all! And why can't Christine marry?" "Because of the Angel of Music,

38
00:04:42.902 --> 00:04:46.871
of course!" "Does he forbid her to marry?" Raoul asked. "He has told her

39
00:04:46.872 --> 00:04:50.678
that if she marries, he will go away forever, and she will never hear him

40
00:04:50.679 --> 00:04:59.573
again. So, you understand, she can't let that happen for the sake of her

41
00:04:59.574 --> 00:05:06.067
career." "Of course," Raoul said, pretending to agree with her. "I thought Christine explained all

42
00:05:06.068 --> 00:05:11.056
this to you in Perros-Guirec, when she was there with the Angel of Music.

43
00:05:11.057 --> 00:05:18.786
He promised to meet her at her father's grave and play some music for

44
00:05:18.787 --> 00:05:24.835
her." "Oh, he met her, did he?" Raoul was growing angrier by the minute. He

45
00:05:25.533 --> 00:05:32.081
was going to have to confront the Angel of Music. "Madame, please tell me

46
00:05:32.082 --> 00:05:39.715
where this angel lives." Mama Valerius raised her eyes and said, "Why in heaven,

47
00:05:39.716 --> 00:05:49.022
of course. That’s where all angels live." Raoul didn't know exactly who this Angel of

48
00:05:49.023 --> 00:05:56.334
Music was but recognized the type of person. "He's some handsome tenor, who's taking

49
00:05:56.335 --> 00:06:01.937
advantage of Christine!" Raoul thought. "He's learned enough about her to know she'd be susceptible

50
00:06:01.938 --> 00:06:08.439
to anything that involved her father and the supernatural." Raoul was filled with despair.

51
00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:14.384
"How long has Christine known this fellow?" Mama Valerius thought for a moment. "I'd

52
00:06:14.385 --> 00:06:22.196
say it's been three months since he started giving her lessons. He used to come

53
00:06:22.197 --> 00:06:28.812
down from heaven and teach her early in the morning in her dressing room.

54
00:06:29.214 --> 00:06:38.513
But now that she has gone away with him, I don't know where her

55
00:06:38.514 --> 00:06:45.743
lessons are. I don’t think he’s taken her to heaven." In great distress, Raoul bid

56
00:06:45.744 --> 00:06:51.098
farewell to Mama Valerius and walked to his brother's house. Philippe was waiting for

57
00:06:51.099 --> 00:06:55.886
him, and Raoul fell into his arms like a child. The count consoled him

58
00:06:55.887 --> 00:07:00.766
without asking for any explanations. How could Raoul even begin to explain the Angel of

59
00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:07.133
Music anyway? "Let's go out to dinner," Philippe said. "I have a strange story

60
00:07:07.134 --> 00:07:13.667
to tell you. Last night Christine was seen behind the racetrack grandstand in the park

61
00:07:13.668 --> 00:07:18.035
on the western edge of Paris." "What? What was she doing in such a

62
00:07:18.036 --> 00:07:27.179
lonely place at night?" "Riding in a carriage with the window down, apparently taking in the night air. She was with a man, a shadowy figure . . ."

63
00:07:28.075 --> 00:07:36.973
Raoul groaned. "Yes, let's have dinner. I need to forget about Christine." But at

64
00:07:36.974 --> 00:07:41.480
the restaurant, Christine was all Raoul thought about. By ten o'clock, he was in

65
00:07:41.481 --> 00:07:48.089
a horse-drawn cab, heading for the road behind the racetrack in the park. "Wait for

66
00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:54.954
me nearby," Raoul said to the driver when they arrived. "I may be awhile."

67
00:07:54.955 --> 00:08:03.638
Bright moonlight illuminated the deserted road. It was bitterly cold, and Raoul stamped his feet

68
00:08:03.639 --> 00:08:13.364
to keep warm. He'd been waiting for half an hour when a carriage turned

69
00:08:13.365 --> 00:08:16.340
